		{"id":"plateau-example","type":"file","file":"skills/common-workflow/architecture/example_architecture/plateau/example/plateau-example.skill.md","x":6600,"y":20,"width":340,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"plateau-label","type":"text","text":"**When the plateau appears**\n\nOnly once every solution exists — including `solution-condition-ownership`, which contributes no code but is still required (see the plateau's own ADR). The plateau is the last stage, never a peer of the solutions/groups to its left.","x":6560,"y":-160,"width":380,"height":140},
		{"id":"callout-exception","type":"text","text":"**Narrow cross-group exception**\n\n`solution-domain-rule` (domain-modeling) `depends_on` `solution-transport-validation` (request-handling) directly — the red edge below. This points the *opposite* way from the green group-level edge, because it records a file-level fact (`domain-rule` extends a file `transport-validation` already created), not the conceptual group ordering. See `solution-domain-rule`'s own `# Requirements` section.","x":2980,"y":80,"width":460,"height":260},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"**Legend**\n\n- Black edge — solution-level `depends_on` (prerequisite → dependent, reverse of the YAML)\n- Red edge — the one narrow cross-group solution edge, justified by a concrete `Implementation/*.extend.md` target\n- Green edge — group-level `depends_on` (conceptual: every request-handling solution needs domain-modeling's types to exist)\n- Cyan edges — every solution feeding into `plateau-example` at assembly time\n\nGroup boxes are visual only (Obsidian Canvas groups); membership is also declared in each group skill's `contains:` frontmatter.","x":0,"y":900,"width":620,"height":300}
	],
